SPURS stale task exit drops its lock-line reservation context (CASPER-3)

USER: the game crashed at the end of Survival (and at 03:10 in user-play5):
SIGSEGV in spu_coh_notify_write (spu_coherency.c:196) on the PPU loading
thread, right after "[spu_workload] task N of shut-down taskset ...: ending
its thread". 0069's spu_task_exit_stale ends a stale task with pthread_exit /
ExitThread from inside WAIT_SIGNAL, which skips spu_run_lifted_job_abi's
spu_coh_unregister: the fur task's (image 9) stack-local spu_context stayed in
s_coh_ctxs, and the next PPU store to a line it had reserved walked the freed
stack. spu_async_run now records a stack mark, and spu_task_exit_stale drops
every reserver context between its frame and that mark (spu_coh_forget_range,
under the lock-line lock) before ending the thread.
c3-stale1 (closed-loop, build-casper): tutorial -> quit to title -> tutorial
-> quit, twice the exact log sequence of the crash; each time
"[spu-coh] leaked ctx ... (img=9) dropped at thread exit" for both fur tasks,
no crash, fur renders after the tasksets are re-created; 0 FATAL, 0 LIFT-GAP.

